course: dictionary
lesson: 2275
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word creek can mean different things in different places. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. In «Kiri in Rotorua said nothing when her mum asked about the storm; she and her friend had gone to the creek, which flooded», the word flooded tells you the creek holds water, so it is a small stream.
explain: Now read «Toad then rows the Rat's boat to the boat-house creek». Rowing a boat and a boat-house tell you the creek is a narrow inlet where water comes in from the sea or a river. Ask yourself: what would make sense here? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Creek can also be part of an idiom. If someone says they are «up the creek», they are not near water at all. The idiom means they are in trouble. Idioms have meanings you cannot work out word by word, so context and a dictionary are your best helpers.
fact: A creek is a small stream or narrow river in the US, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: In the UK, a creek is a narrow inlet where the sea or a river comes into the land.
fact: «Up the creek» is slang meaning in trouble.
fact: Many creeks in Australia dry up in summer, so their meaning depends on the place and the season.
fact: Creeks can flood fast after rain, so «a flooding creek» is dangerous and you should never play beside one.
exercise: «She and her friend had gone to the creek, which flooded.» What is a creek here? | *A small stream or narrow river | A loud school bell | A tall hill covered in trees | A kind of sandwich
exercise: «Toad then rows the Rat's boat to the boat-house creek.» What kind of place is a creek here? | A mountain path | A school playground | *A narrow inlet where water comes into the land | A busy road with lots of cars
exercise: Jayden says, «I lost my bike key and I'm late. I'm up the creek!» What does up the creek mean? | Happy and singing | Good at swimming | *In trouble | Right beside a river
test: «A secret about danger, like playing by a flooding creek, is not yours to keep.» Why is a flooding creek dangerous? | *Water can rise fast and sweep people away | Its ice is too thin to skate on | Fish bite anyone who swims there | It is full of sweets
test: «Weeks later Mum found muddy jandals with creek weed on them.» What are jandals? | Gloves | Hats | *Flip-flops | Socks
exam: Which clue in «the creek had swept a dog away that day» shows a creek can be dangerous? | Kiri has a friend | Mum found the jandals | Toad rows the boat | *Swept a dog away
